@model CreateOrderItemViewModel

<h2>Create New OrderItem</h2>
@*
    Why "OrderItem." in front of everything?

    The model is not an OrderItem anymore. It's a ViewModel — a box that holds:
      - an OrderItem   (the thing we're filling in)
      - two lists      (the options for the dropdowns)

    asp-for always starts looking inside the model (the box).
    The box doesn't have an ItemId — the OrderItem inside the box does.
    So we write the path: first OrderItem, then ItemId → "OrderItem.ItemId".

    Like a folder path: Box / OrderItem / ItemId

    ("Member variable" in the demo text just means "something that lives inside".)
*@

@*
A ViewModel is a class made for one page. It holds exactly what that page needs, nothing more.

It exists because of one rule: a view can only take one @model. Usually a page needs more than one thing, so you pack them into one class and send that.

Model vs ViewModel

Model (Item, OrderItem) = the shape of your data. Matches a database table.
ViewModel = the shape of a page. Built only to carry stuff to a view. Never stored in the database (no DbSet for it).*@
<form asp-action="CreateOrderItem">
    <div class="form-group">
        <label asp-for="OrderItem.ItemId"></label><span class="text-danger">*</span>
        <select asp-for="OrderItem.ItemId" asp-items="Model.ItemSelectList" class="form-control">
            <option value="">Select an item...</option>
        </select>
        <span asp-validation-for="OrderItem.ItemId" class="text-danger"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
        <label asp-for="OrderItem.Quantity"></label><span class="text-danger">*</span>
        <input asp-for="OrderItem.Quantity" class="form-control" />
        <span asp-validation-for="OrderItem.Quantity" class="text-danger"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
        <label asp-for="OrderItem.OrderId"></label><span class="text-danger">*</span>
        <select asp-for="OrderItem.OrderId" asp-items="Model.OrderSelectList" class="form-control">
            <option value="">Select an order...</option>
        </select>
        <span asp-validation-for="OrderItem.OrderId" class="text-danger"></span>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Create</button>
    <a asp-action="Table" class="btn btn-secondary">Back to Order Table</a>
</form>